      "title" = "The Dragon issue-10 opener, part two - the Gilbert dungeon method article (folios 11-14), the Weights & Measures article (folios 19-20) and the Holsinger level ritual article (folios 20-21): three adjudicated chains and the part-one flip",
      "provenance" = "Pinned from The Dragon Vol. 2 No. 4 (October 1977), the archive.org scan voice (single-voice; the source lives in the archive.org item accessory-dragon-magazine-012). The folios: 11-14, the Gilbert Design Forum dungeon-method article - think like the builders and allow every necessary function, the organized society that dug the dungeon out of solid rock and then abandoned it, the rooms no longer used for their intention and read like antedated storefronts, the builder occupation, standing, alignment and personality decreeing the levels, the storage-room rule, the two views - vertical cutaway and horizontal overlay at 200 feet to the inch - keep it simple and stick to a plan, the rich-builder doctrine, and the Nappo dig: 120 years of life, 275 years dead, three facets and fifteen levels, the report 010 box label reading 11-13 against the article tail riding folio 14 beside the Archive ad; 19-20, the Crabaugh Weights & Measures article - Size on 3d6 and Build on d6, +1 hit per die at Size 16 and up, -1 at 5 and down, one pound at 10 GP, armor at 15, 30 and 60 percent of body mass, females +2 Constitution and +1 Dexterity with the lighter carrying capacity, the musculature-versus-force doctrine, the carrying grid - human 1.0 to 3.0, dwarf 1.5 to 3.5, hobbit 2.0 to 4.0 in tenths of body weight, the elf column mirroring the human, the speed ladder at 3, 6, 9 and 12, the male height-and-weight grid from 5-1 and 120 pounds to 6-4 and 215, the female grid from 4-10 and 100 to 6-1 and 185, and the appearance bands - eyes, hair, skin, voice, handedness, expression, hair length, males at 30 percent bearded; 20-21, the Holsinger Gaining a New Experience Level article - the four-part ritual of qualification, attention, intercession and exhaustion, the good fasting and prayer or the sacrifice at double the new level with each creature at least half and conscious, the 50/50 neutral notice and the 50/50 evil nothing, the 60/40 sacrilege chances and the 50% temple-rite kill, the druid tree at 1 hit die and mistletoe at 10, the neutral mistletoe tree rite with its free cure, the Great Pink Elephants in the drunken stupor, the demihuman liquor toughness behind the level limits, the 7th-level militia ejection and the guild halls, and the spell learning by the Greyhawk columns with one forgettable spell per level. The part-one box in report 010 flips closed this round, 1 closed / 1 open. PRINT FOLIO = PDF PAGE, verified at the printed 10, 19 and 21 footers.",
      "sentinel" = "The variant-layer doctrine holds: Dragon ink is never core 1e canon, and the Holsinger level ritual and the Crabaugh Size system - though both echo later print - pin as a variant layer with provenance, never core canon. The print quirks ride AS SCANNED, noted, never silent: the male medium-weight Size-4 cell reading 185 as scanned against the 135 column pattern; the female Size-15 height cell garbled and riding sentinel -1; the carrying grid elf column mirroring the human with its two garbled cells riding the transcript, the dwarf Strength-16 cell garbled and riding sentinel; the speed-12 fraction garbled in the OCR, the speed pinning and the fraction riding; the facial-features d6-minus-2 rule and the limb tables riding prose; the Snits game and the Stellar Conquest article scoped out as other systems. The editor's standing caution rides: none of this is official.",
    },
